export anchor WeatherForecastStyle:
    number: 75
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Weather forecast
    idea: The dashboard is the evening weather map, with projects placed as towns carrying a sun, cloud or rain symbol and a big temperature-style percent, and the overdue count shown as a storm warning.
    base: light
    palette:
        sky: #e6f2fb, the page, fading down from #cfe6f7 at the top
        card: #ffffff, panels, reading tiles and town cards
        sea: #d4e8f6, map water
        land: #e5eed6, map land, with #d9e6c6 for hills
        isobar: #8fb0c9, pressure lines on the map, decoration only
        nightInk: #0f2a44, text and the bulletin time tabs
        haze: #40607b, meta text and the cloud outline
        studioBlue: #1757a6, panel header bars, buttons, the current nav pill, the cold front and focus
        sunshine: #f2b51d, sun fill, always outlined in #6a4800
        fairGreen: #1c6a36, the On track word
        overcastAmber: #7f4f00, the At risk word
        stormRed: #ad2219, the Behind word, the warning edge, the low pressure L and the overdue count
    type:
        One rounded broadcast sans, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. The greeting is 40px at 800 with tight tracking, reading
        numbers 46px at 800, town percents 36px at 800 with a 15px percent
        sign raised like a degree, panel headers 17px at 800 in white on
        blue, body 16px, meta 12px at 600 and status words 12px at 800 in
        caps.
    layout:
        A channel bar holds a sun logo with Brightwork and Project outlook,
        nav as pills in a translucent white capsule with Home filled blue,
        then a round search, a New project pill, a round bell with a red
        count and a sun-yellow avatar for Mara Okafor. The presenter strip
        pairs the big greeting and date with a white Storm warning card that
        has a red left edge, a red triangle with a lightning bolt and 4
        tasks are overdue. Four reading tiles follow with a weather glyph
        and a big number each. The main row has a wide Project map panel, a
        sea and land map with isobars, a red L and a blue H and cold and
        warm fronts, with six white town cards placed over it, each with a
        glyph, the big percent, name, a status word with a weather phrase
        and a meta line, and a legend strip below. Beside it Latest
        bulletins are lower-third bands with a dark time tab. A full-width
        14-day record line chart follows, last week dashed grey, this week
        solid red with a shaded area and the value over every point, and
        tags for 59, 73 and the peak. At 375px the town cards stack as a
        list over the map and the chart scrolls inside its panel.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12 to 20px between tiles and panels and 14 to 18px inside.
    density: Low to medium. Big readings with compact town cards on the map.
    corners: Round and soft, 18px panels, 14 to 16px tiles and town cards, pills for nav and buttons.
    borders: Almost none. A blue header bar tops each panel and the warning has an 8px red left edge.
    shadows: Soft 0 6px 18px shadows in navy at 8 percent under panels, a little stronger under town cards.
    icons:
        Forecast glyphs drawn with dark outlines. A sun with rays for On
        track, a cloud over a sun for At risk, a dark cloud with rain for
        Behind and a red triangle with a bolt for overdue, each beside its
        word.
    focus: A 3px studio blue outline offset 2px.
    tone: A friendly presenter, such as Storm warning, conditions now, sunny, clouding over and heavy rain.
